Revision history for Lilith

4.0.0	unreleased
		 - Schema version 3 -> 11; run lilith migrate after upgrading.
		 - search(): the class, string, and address filters take several
		   values, positives ORed and negations ANDed, with '%' LIKE
		   support per item. proto, event_id, and the hashes moved to
		   the string handling, so they take those as well. lilith -a
		   search: -c may be repeated or comma separated.
		 - search(): fix multi-value numeric filters being ORed instead
		   of ANDed, so e.g. dest_port "!22, !443" filtered nothing.
		 - search(): the port and ip filters take '!' negation, the
		   comparison operators, and comma separated values.
		 - search(): an explicit start/end window as an alternative to
		   go_back_minutes, ranged on the type's time column.
		 - The web search page submits every text filter as one
		   parameter per value, so each gets its own chip above the
		   results and can be dropped without clearing the rest. A
		   filter named after a groupable column offers the values that
		   occur, with counts, from /api/search/values. Its When control
		   -- last N minutes or a custom range -- is a shared partial
		   used on /logs and /dashboard too.
		 - Widen cape_alerts.malscore to double precision; CAPE's
		   malscore is fractional and aborted the INSERT.
		 - Ingest Baphomet's judgment EVE into a new baphomet_alerts
		   table, wired into search, the CLI, Lilith::Stats, and the
		   dashboard. Lilith::Receiver takes it over both transports,
		   its events can be escalated manually and automatically
		   (though it is kept out of the default rule-tables set, so a
		   rule only acts on it when it says so), and a per-instance
		   baphomet_event_ignore drops chosen event types.
		 - Add a configurable web dashboard at /dashboard. Widgets --
		   stat, top values, over time, and source countries -- drag
		   and resize on a 12-column Gridstack and persist in a new
		   dashboards table as one shared board, the web UI being
		   unauthenticated. Each picks its table, column, and measure
		   (sum, average, or a distinct count) from a per-table
		   catalog, including virtual suricata dimensions dug out of
		   the raw EVE: severity, and the MITRE ATT&CK tactic and
		   technique a ruleset tags on. The time window and bucket are
		   set per board and overridable per widget, and "Reset to..."
		   seeds one of the built-in presets. Backed by Lilith::Stats
		   and /api/dashboard/*, drawn with a vendored Chart.js and
		   documented in docs/dashboard.md.
		 - Add Lilith::Stats, the aggregation layer behind it: total,
		   distinct, top, and bucketed timeseries over the alert
		   tables. Names are checked against a fixed set and the window
		   and limit integer-checked, so request parameters pass
		   straight through.
		 - Add a read-only /logs page for browsing an Allani store
		   (syslog, http_access, http_error, and an interleaved http
		   view) over its own [allani] connection, so the two need not
		   share a database. Hidden unless [allani] is configured.
		   Dashboard widgets and presets can read a log source as well
		   as an alert table, and the event view gains a Logs dropdown
		   deep-linking around the event.
		 - Add search and dashboard indexes; the alert tables carried
		   only their primary key, so anything filtered or aggregated
		   seq-scanned.
		 - Add lilith deploy / migrate / schema_version wrapping
		   DBIx::Class::Migration, so the schema is handled with the
		   same CLI and config as everything else.
		 - Fix the migration fixture directories never installing.
		   ExtUtils::Install hardcodes skipping .exists, so the
		   placeholder is now named keep.
		 - Add mojo_lilith_receiver (Lilith::Receiver), which ingests
		   alert rows a sensor pushes to /eve/:table over HTTP POST or
		   a WebSocket, so sensors need no database credentials -- the
		   receiving side of App::Lilu's push modes. Bodies are
		   validated against the table's columns; id, escalations, and
		   auto_escalated cannot be set by a caller. API keys are
		   stored as their SHA-256 and managed with the lilith
		   receiver_key_* commands, and may be scoped to client
		   IPs/subnets and to instance names, which take the '*' and
		   '?' wildcards.
		 - Rename init/ to rc/, split into rc/freebsd/ and rc/systemd/,
		   and add boot scripts for both Mojolicious daemons.
		 - Add escalation. Targets live in SQL and have a pluggable
		   type under Lilith::Escalate::Type:: (Webhook, Email, and
		   Syslog ship). The web UI gains a /escalation management
		   page, an Escalate button and history on the event view, and
		   an "E" badge in search results; the CLI gains esc,
		   esc_history, esc_types, and the esc_target_* actions. Every
		   attempt is recorded with its status and the payload actually
		   sent, and the alert tables gain an escalations bigint[] so a
		   reader sees escalation counts without a join. The web side
		   is gated behind escalation_enable, with sends run in a
		   subprocess; the CLI is not, as it already holds the DB
		   credentials.
		 - Add automatic escalation. Rules are a JSON match/actions DSL
		   in a new auto_escalations table, compiled by
		   Lilith::AutoEscalate into a Rule::Engine ruleset and
		   evaluated by auto_escalate() against recently ingested
		   alerts, escalating through the same audit trail. Each alert
		   gains an auto_escalated timestamp so it is considered once,
		   and a stop_on_match rule halts later rules for it. Adds the
		   lilith auto_escalate and ae_* actions plus rc/ service,
		   timer, and cron examples, and a /auto_escalation page with a
		   visual match builder and a live dry-run preview. Editing
		   rules from the web needs auto_escalation_manage_enable, off
		   by default.
		 - EVE instances are now defined under [eves.*]; old top-level
		   instance tables are ignored, with a warning.
		 - web event view: a Download PCAP control fetches the flow
		   PCAP from a remote Virani instance ([virani.NAME] tables),
		   lets you pick the set, and can hand you a virani command to
		   run on the PCAP box instead. The fetch runs in a subprocess.
		 - web: a Virani navbar dropdown searches a remote for a BPF
		   filter and time range, or browses its recent cached searches
		   when virani_search_enable is on. It always builds a copyable
		   local virani command; downloading through the web server is
		   what the option gates.
		 - web: /api/ipinfo and /api/domaininfo run their blocking work
		   in a subprocess.
		 - web: an HTTPS button under Domain Info checks
		   https://DOMAIN:PORT/ and reports the status, per-phase
		   timing, and as much certificate detail as possible. 5s
		   timeout and 512KB read cap, both noted when hit.
		 - web: a Mail button under Domain Info runs SPF, DMARC, and
		   DKIM checks, probing common selectors when none is given.
		 - Lilith->run() warns and skips a malformed EVE instance
		   instead of dying.
		 - Add a docs/ dir matching the rest of the LilithSec
		   household, and rework the README to a short intro pointing
		   at docs/index.md.
		 - Fix the sagan_alerts INSERT listing "proto" twice, which
		   PostgreSQL rejects.
		 - Factor the EVE field extraction out of the run() POE closure
		   into a testable parse_eve(), with %Lilith::alert_columns as
		   the shared source of truth for each table's column order.
		 - replace TOML with TOML::Tiny

3.0.0	2026-06-25/01:00
		 - use DBIx::Class::Migration
		 - use dbic-migration for migration DB schema versioning and updating
		 - really needs PostgreSQL for jsonb
		 - a few more real basic tests

2.0.0	2026-03-20/23:00
